  - created_at: "2026-07-24T12:10:46.948Z"
    author: claude-code-agent
    text: "Current whole-system roadmap evidence: live review covered 1,926 pre-mutation items and 32,963 history events; the full CLI and SDK architecture, 75-name root surface, token shapes, exact 100% coverage, zero local code clones, security/dependency gates, effective LOC and folder fan-out, semantic merge/storage invariants, open concurrency races, current GitHub/npm state, and all 18 official external repositories/packages. Existing canonical owners absorbed broad findings. Only two focused gaps were added: pm-hcrmye for the reproduced 10k create/claim latency-RSS regression and pm-feecbs for fleet-wide external package conformance. Completed evidence plan pm-xe0c38 contains sequencing and linked proof. Substantive tracker-only publication is b7bb0db6ab8c5cb637425e1ce52b020b02cfe7ae on main."
  - created_at: "2026-07-25T22:11:02.472Z"
    author: "harness:opencode"
    text: "Ecosystem review 2026-07-25 (night) — all-status organization, directive-theme coverage verification, and strategic-graph deepening. Pre-mutation baseline: 2,042 items (264 open, 1,766 closed, 12 canceled), 34,347 immutable history events across 2,052 streams; validate clean except the canonical owned warning class (resolution fields, 287, owned by pm-e9zh/pm-wenq); history drift 0; health green; dedupe-audit shows only the known canceled probe cluster; graph 2,045 nodes / 4,523 edges / 0 active isolates / 0 active degree-one nodes.\n\nDirective coverage map (each requested theme verified against live canonical owners; no territory-level gaps found, so no umbrella items were created): CLI simplification -> pm-n7rr + grammar gates pm-wt43zj/pm-fs8q9x + milestone pm-j82fd3; token-efficient output -> pm-5t33or/pm-cxr0jb/pm-kvxqp1/pm-mav1ak/pm-cha95z + gate pm-cu1i; context algorithms for 3-item to 1M-item workspaces -> pm-4k6b catalog (24) + pm-g8t7b9 registry + pm-7ob5 analytics + pm-atfm harness + spectrum pair pm-z436/pm-g2zz; thousands of concurrent agents + conflict-free branch merging -> pm-dj98/pm-3oqjnc/pm-lvyd/pm-76dnfg/pm-2sbj8p + defects pm-c0wthb/pm-9j2r3b/pm-z8qd4k; immutable restorable history -> pm-w7ccmv + pm-9yfo/pm-3z0k/pm-u14c/pm-wlqxg3/pm-5gf0xf; SDK-first with CLI as a thin layer -> pm-usfg + milestone pm-9rgaal; universal customization and beyond-PM domains (VCS, companies, digital twins) -> pm-8jdc/pm-t4d7nz/pm-iiv1gl/pm-8ngt/pm-kr3t/pm-g608fc/pm-mj42og; grep/jq composability -> pm-m9xv/pm-646c/pm-psy1; extremely critical CI/CD -> pm-zclzll/pm-rtn5h6/pm-a8lnoh/pm-pae3wo/pm-76dnfg/pm-k6t4yb/pm-kpftft/pm-zlv8jl; all-status deep relationship graph -> pm-96h7/pm-a8zm/pm-qnl2/pm-lnrk/pm-hnc9w7/pm-s5e04g/pm-bzmeaa; long-range planning -> six-milestone ladder to 2028-06-30 plus the post-ladder horizon-themes note on this item.\n\nFiled this pass (one, dedupe-checked): pm-zeifd2 — pass-identifier convention (date+theme, never sequential numbers), the single directive not yet tracked anywhere.\n\nGraph deepening this pass (typed, evidence-backed only): epic-executes-milestone implements edges pm-o2kc->pm-w7ccmv, pm-n7rr->pm-j82fd3, pm-usfg->pm-9rgaal, pm-9rxu->pm-o87av6; proof edges pm-u14c verifies pm-w7ccmv and pm-iiv1gl verifies pm-t4d7nz; component edges on the closed pm-klo8 (verifies pm-w7ccmv plus sibling component links) with a disclosure comment — that mutation touched a terminal item because the roadmap prose naming it was stale; retained per the superseding-event rule and recorded as a process lesson (verify live status before every mutation). Active-set semantic reachability from the six outcome milestones remains complete; the known terminal-only deficit stays owned by pm-lnrk under its changelog-safe batch strategy and was deliberately not swept here."
  - created_at: "2026-07-26T10:32:00.898Z"
    author: "harness:opencode"
    text: "Ecosystem review 2026-07-26 (theme: agent-context readiness; pass identifier per decision pm-zeifd2 — date+theme, no sequential numbers). Tracker-only manual audit of the full pm CLI, public SDK, repo architecture, agent UX, performance, security, code quality, tests, docs, skills, bundled+external packages on current main; evidence plan pm-t9e3bc. Pre-mutation baseline: 2,066 items, health 0 warnings, history drift 0, single known warning class validate_resolution_missing_fields:288 (owned by pm-e9zh).\n\nGATES (all green on main): pnpm build; pnpm lint (eslint --max-warnings=0, jscpd 0 clones across 730 TS files / 417,755 lines, static-quality, package-boundary, token-budget 14 surfaces, SDK surface snapshot 0 classified changes, SDK import-cost 10 entrypoints, CLI transport floor 6 ops); docs-skills gate; focused suite tests/unit/sdk/sdk-index.spec.ts 129/129. One cold-run false failure of the import-cost gate (545>510ms on ./sdk/runtime, immediate warm re-run green) filed as NEW pm-cg1sjb — the only non-duplicate finding of the pass.\n\nLATENCY at 2,066 items (evidence on pm-ag9nka): context 1.1-1.3s, search 1.0-1.2s, list-open 0.74-0.92s, get 0.64-0.88s, --version 57ms. pm-801d read index is the reliever; framing upgraded from pure-scale to daily agent-perceived latency.\n\nSURFACE CENSUSES: 74 top-level contract spellings / 88 help lines incl. alias pairs / 7 extensions loaded with 21 command handlers (evidence+correction on pm-n7rr); SDK 3,113 symbols across 10 entrypoints, 923 advanced_export-tier (evidence on pm-usfg, pm-te6elw); extension-loaded help/contracts payloads already exceed fixture budgets (evidence on pm-z71aoy).\n\nVERIFIED HEALTHY (no item needed): structured error recovery with recovery bundles + RFC-7807 JSON mode + correct exit codes (2/3) + did-you-mean id suggestions — agent never hard-blocked; merge drivers installed (pm merge install fence intact); npm 2026.7.26 live and all 8 external packages in sync; 13 first-party packages zero-runtime-deps; DeepScan/CodeFactor/DeepSource configs all active (branch protection), no legacy dotfiles found; root .deepscan.json/.deepsource.toml/.codefactor.yml confirmed in-use, not debris; docs/skills duplication gate green; merge conformance (pm-76dnfg) and ecosystem conformance (pm-feecbs) already tracked; GH-issue spot checks map 1:1 (GH-714->pm-5sm91o, GH-711->pm-cragzs).\n\nDIRECTIVE-THEME COVERAGE (all pre-owned, no umbrella filed): simplification pm-n7rr + ADR pm-pbyu; SDK-first pm-usfg; token efficiency pm-5t33or/pm-z71aoy/pm-cu1i; instant-feel pm-801d/pm-ag9nka/pm-9rxu; multi-agent merge pm-dj98/pm-76dnfg/pm-a8lnoh; repo organization pm-kb5h/pm-yh8r/pm-ld0z under pm-92if; dead code pm-f4yn; gate reliability pm-k6t4yb (+new pm-cg1sjb); graph pm-96h7; context engine pm-4k6b; beyond-PM exemplars pm-8ngt/pm-xtrd/pm-kr3t."
  - created_at: "2026-07-26T11:00:18.513Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Reconciliation 2026-07-26 (agent-legibility and provable-history review). Seven items filed, every one duplicate-checked against the full corpus and reproduced against the shipped 2026.7.26 build.\n\nProvable history: pm-10l1vm — recorded entries carry no branch-independent ordering identity, so causal order across concurrently written streams is reconstructed from wall-clock time alone; it now blocks the convergence ADR pm-2sbj8p. pm-bbk8we — the integrity chain hard-codes SHA-256 with no algorithm field, leaving the proof no migration path; it now blocks the portable attestation pm-3z0k. Both sit under pm-o2kc and verify pm-w7ccmv. Horizon: 4-plus, but both are cheaper now than after every additional entry is written without the field.\n\nGovernance and data quality: pm-pcys9n — release attribution derives from a mutable timestamp while the stable release key is populated with values that cannot match a tag; it now blocks pm-e9zh, pm-pivf and pm-lnrk, which is the real reason the terminal-graph backfill has been expensive rather than merely risky. pm-pj2isb — a historical bulk backfill wrote one repeated literal into six fields across hundreds of terminal items, inflating every completeness metric and feeding constant-valued features to the relevance engine. Horizon: near, because the terminal graph program is gated behind the first.\n\nDelivery quality: pm-lpqln4 — the bunx published-artifact check passes with an arbitrary token in the executable position, verified against the published build, and no install path is exercised for any package manager. pm-ei6x66 — local and hosted verification are two independently maintained gate sets with no parity contract. pm-okgxwa — ranking explanation is sized by the workspace rather than by the answer: explaining two rows emits one entry per active item, 131 KB against 1.8 KB, and the token budget has no effect on it. Horizon: near.\n\nTracker state after the pass: validate warning classes reduced from seven to four, with the merge fence re-installed, both active-terminal-parent rows re-parented onto live epics with lineage preserved, and every missing estimate filled. All 275 non-milestone active items now reach an outcome milestone through typed implements or verifies paths at a maximum distance of five, with no isolated and no degree-one active nodes. The four remaining warning classes are the known legacy faucets owned by pm-j8z6, pm-pivf, pm-e9zh and pm-wenq, and three of the four are now explicitly gated behind pm-pcys9n."
  - created_at: "2026-07-29T04:55:03.616Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Shippable first tranche of horizon Q filed as pm-sxyj1v: the behavioural-constant inventory and the labelling gate. It is deliberately scoped to declaring and gating rather than retuning, so it can close without the multi-scale corpus suite existing, and it makes the scale conformance work on pm-m2il meaningful when that lands because a calibrated constant will then have a named corpus to be recalibrated against."
  - created_at: "2026-07-29T21:30:26.047Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Delivery evidence for the 2026-07-29 ecosystem planning refresh: 14 active records that had rich goals but empty descriptions now have concise scope descriptions; nine canonical roadmap owners carry detailed planning architecture for command simplification, SDK-first migration, context ranking, concurrency, immutable history, CI/release, RL/evals, and graph algorithms; five existing issue/task owners carry live validation evidence; eight strategic pairs gained typed blocked_by prerequisites, replacing two generic related edges. No new item was created because exact, high-confidence fuzzy, and parent-scope duplicate review found every requested theme already had a canonical owner.\n\nPost-change checks: 308 open items have zero missing descriptions, acceptance criteria, estimates, or relationships; no item is in progress; graph nodes 2,200, edges 9,942, one connected component, zero active isolates, zero active nodes of degree one or less; the critical execution path is now 9 edges across 10 layers and remains evidence-based; graph audit has only the same 11 informational legacy findings owned by pm-hnc9w7; validation checked all 2,197 items with zero history drift or chain errors and only the known 292 terminal resolution warnings owned by pm-e9zh; build passed; generated changelog is unchanged and check-clean; published-release verification passed npm, direct and package-selected npx, bunx, and GitHub Release for 2026.7.29. All writes were automatically attributed to harness:codex without PM_AUTHOR or --author."
    edited_at: "2026-07-29T21:30:47.005Z"
  - created_at: "2026-07-31T10:17:20.830Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Portfolio organization 2026-07-31: the live tracker already covers every directive in the request through canonical lineages, so no duplicate roadmap umbrella or numbered review item was created. Current outcome paths are explicit: pm-pbyu -> pm-0z7n -> command-family consolidations -> pm-1kxs -> pm-j82fd3 for agent-legible grammar; pm-usfg -> pm-9rgaal for SDK completeness; pm-vvib/pm-g8t7b9 + pm-atfm -> pm-4k6b -> pm-tch9cs/pm-2sbj8p -> pm-o87av6 for quality-preserving scale; pm-9yfo -> pm-w7ccmv for restorable immutable proof; release timing/guard/ledger issues -> pm-e70zh5 plus pm-ygli86/pm-zclzll/pm-rtn5h6/pm-pae3wo -> pm-xp1xsw for GA; and pm-li2fj5/pm-nfrhf0 + pm-8jdc + GA -> pm-t4d7nz for universal domain and RL/eval use. Horizons remain evidence-gated through pm-m08hza rather than calendar promises."
