    text: "Ecosystem audit #10 (2026-07-06, full all-status manual review, 1563 items): ONE structural gap found and filed — pm-9x6e (capstone: zero the 91-entry SDK import-boundary baseline, flip MCP layer to SDK, harden ratchet to hard-deny; deps on all 8 pm-usfg promotion items). Organization fixes: parented the last 2 orphans pm-p5u6 + pm-tgq6 under pm-u9d0. Verified live: all 20 open GH issues map 1:1 to pm items (GH-455 fix shipped as pm-aems — triage closure folded into pm-7cx8); all 5 validate warning classes map to open items (pm-j8z6 146+129 file links, pm-e9zh 269 resolution + 18 close-reason incl. new pm-muhw entry, pm-pivf dup issue-code); pm-rjqr correctly stays in_progress (PR #466 shipped SDK read primitives, CLI-handler flip is the remaining AC); docstring epic pm-4ak1 lanes active; auto-release healthy (2026.7.4/5/6 all on npm). Simplification epic pm-n7rr: all 64 command spellings have exactly one grammar home (ADR pm-pbyu addendum), dependency graph fully wired (clusters -> pm-0z7n shim -> ADR), zero new clusters needed. SDK-first epic pm-usfg: all 8 domain promotions + exemplar + docs + boundary gate present; pm-9x6e was the only missing terminal piece. Active-item metadata 100% (body/AC/risk/confidence/priority/estimate)."
