    text: "Planning/review pass 2026-07-07 (evening) summary: (1) Reconciliation — release v2026.7.7 verified live on npm+GitHub; all open GH issues map 1:1 to open pm items; GH-455 closed upstream with PR#464 evidence (pm-aems already closed with matching resolution); dependabot PRs 462/465 green, 462 auto-merge armed by owner; all four in_progress items active today under codex-agent (SDK-first lane, not phantom WIP). (2) Drift — resolution 269, close_reason 18, files 147/125: all four counts stable vs previous pass; recorded on pm-e9zh/pm-j8z6. (3) Brainstorming — pm-4k6b gained the concrete scorer-algorithm note (ACT-R scale-free activation, spreading activation over typed+semantic edges, learned-but-linear signal weights against pm-atfm, submodular token-budget packing); pm-vvib gained mind-model subsystem candidate #5 theory-of-mind/common-ground (receiver-watermark handoff briefs + expertise routing; items only on ADR acceptance). (4) New items — pm-a9mc validate counts-only projection (token-efficiency; related to pm-cfed) and pm-b84u repeated --ac last-wins bug (uncovered remainder of the pm-cf1u/pm-6mit class, reproduced live on v2026.7.7). No items closed this pass, so no changelog impact. Next executable remains pm-m4iu (P1 closed_at stamp); SDK-first lane continues under codex-agent."
  - created_at: "2026-07-07T15:26:31.853Z"
    author: maintainer-agent
    text: "Planning review pass 2026-07-07 (30th, second follow-up today): live baseline ok (validate ok, 193 open / 4 legitimately-active WIP under pm-usfg by codex-agent, all updated same-day). Reconciliation clean: PR#478 (pm-alnj GH-474, pm-5h9g GH-476) and PR#479 (pm-6abs GH-467) all closed with evidence; every open GH issue (435-473) maps to at least one open pm item; GH-209 duplicate-code warning owned by open pm-pivf. Release 2026.7.7 on npm, [Unreleased] empty, auto-release skip legitimate (evidence on pm-7zs0). Validate drift counts steady vs earlier today (147/125/269/18) — no new drift comments filed. New defects filed from pm next hot-path inspection: pm-hfg5 (recommended item duplicated verbatim as ready[0] — token waste on the highest-frequency agent read) and pm-yl6c (recommendation tells callers to resume ANOTHER agent's assigned WIP — caller-aware ranking needed; related pm-114v). Brainstorming: pm-vvib gained candidates #6 source monitoring (derived evidence-class trust grading) and #7 negativity bias (mutation-time cautionary recall of failure episodes); pm-4k6b gained algorithms (5) reciprocal-rank-fusion cold-start combiner and (6) write-time incremental signal maintenance folding scorer state into the derived read index. Next executable remains pm-m4iu (closed_at stamp, P1)."
  - created_at: "2026-07-07T15:37:44.857Z"
